      },
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "## 6. Overfitting vs Underfitting Analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "### Conceptual Overview\n",
        "\n",
        "| Condition | Description | K Value | Symptom |\n",
        "|-----------|-------------|---------|--------|\n",
        "| **Overfitting** | Model memorizes training data including noise | K too small (K=1) | High train accuracy, low test accuracy (large gap) |\n",
        "| **Underfitting** | Model is too simple to capture patterns | K too large (K=29) | Low train AND test accuracy |\n",
        "| **Optimal Fit** | Good generalization to unseen data | K balanced | Both train & test accuracy are high and close |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "f0ZsnAIpRhUs",
        "outputId": "82cf4606-979c-4645-b77d-b773b83cbd63"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Overfitting vs Underfitting Demonstration:\n",
            "----------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
            "  Overfitting (K=1)         => Train: 1.0000 | Test: 0.7541 | Gap: 0.2459\n",
            "  Optimal (K=22)            => Train: 0.8382 | Test: 0.8033 | Gap: 0.0349\n",
            "  Underfitting (K=29)       => Train: 0.8257 | Test: 0.8197 | Gap: 0.0061\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Demonstrate with specific K values\n",
        "demo_ks = {'Overfitting (K=1)': 1, f'Optimal (K={best_k_cv})': best_k_cv, 'Underfitting (K=29)': 29}\n",
        "\n",
        "print('Overfitting vs Underfitting Demonstration:')\n",
        "print('-' * 70)\n",
        "for label, k in demo_ks.items():\n",
        "    knn = KNeighborsClassifier(n_neighbors=k)\n",
        "    knn.fit(X_train_scaled, y_train)\n",
        "    tr_acc = knn.score(X_train_scaled, y_train)\n",
        "    te_acc = knn.score(X_test_scaled, y_test)\n",
        "    gap = tr_acc - te_acc\n",
        "    print(f'  {label:25s} => Train: {tr_acc:.4f} | Test: {te_acc:.4f} | Gap: {gap:.4f}')"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 447
        },
        "id": "hZdbmm2FRhUs",
        "outputId": "21fbe1d1-0494-46cf-d803-bbb24652b056"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1800x500 with 3 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        },
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "\n",
            "Interpretation of Learning Curves:\n",
            "-----------------------------------\n",
            "K=1  (Overfit) : Training score ~ 1.0 but validation score is notably lower.\n",
            "                 Large gap = the model memorizes training data.\n",
            "K=optimal      : Both curves converge at a high accuracy -- good generalization.\n",
            "K=29 (Underfit): Both curves converge at a LOWER accuracy -- model is too simple.\n",
            "\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# --- Learning Curves (diagnose overfitting / underfitting) ---\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(18, 5))\n",
        "\n",
        "for idx, (label, k) in enumerate(demo_ks.items()):\n",
        "    knn = KNeighborsClassifier(n_neighbors=k)\n",
        "    train_sizes, train_lc, val_lc = learning_curve(\n",
        "        knn, X_train_scaled, y_train,\n",
        "        cv=5, scoring='accuracy',\n",
        "        train_sizes=np.linspace(0.1, 1.0, 10),\n",
        "        random_state=42,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    train_mean = train_lc.mean(axis=1)\n",
        "    train_std = train_lc.std(axis=1)\n",
        "    val_mean = val_lc.mean(axis=1)\n",
        "    val_std = val_lc.std(axis=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "    axes[idx].fill_between(train_sizes, train_mean - train_std, train_mean + train_std, alpha=0.15, color='#e74c3c')\n",
        "    axes[idx].fill_between(train_sizes, val_mean - val_std, val_mean + val_std, alpha=0.15, color='#2ecc71')\n",
        "    axes[idx].plot(train_sizes, train_mean, 'o-', color='#e74c3c', label='Training Score', linewidth=2)\n",
        "    axes[idx].plot(train_sizes, val_mean, 's-', color='#2ecc71', label='Validation Score', linewidth=2)\n",
        "    axes[idx].set_xlabel('Training Set Size')\n",
        "    axes[idx].set_ylabel('Accuracy')\n",
        "    axes[idx].set_title(label, fontweight='bold')\n",
        "    axes[idx].legend(loc='lower right')\n",
        "    axes[idx].set_ylim(0.5, 1.05)\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.suptitle('Learning Curves - Diagnosing Overfitting & Underfitting', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold', y=1.02)\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "print('''\n",
        "Interpretation of Learning Curves:\n",
        "-----------------------------------\n",
        "K=1  (Overfit) : Training score ~ 1.0 but validation score is notably lower.\n",
        "                 Large gap = the model memorizes training data.\n",
        "K=optimal      : Both curves converge at a high accuracy -- good generalization.\n",
        "K=29 (Underfit): Both curves converge at a LOWER accuracy -- model is too simple.\n",
        "''')"
      ]
    },
